  "coverage": "The original continuous chart and the winding cutoffs remain in force. A conservative latitude-row union encloses the phase of each eligible source. The interval azimuth query enumerates intersecting 2*pi lifts with outward rounding and longitude key padding. The resulting visits are counted before the per-star filters. The original exact screen predicates then decide each candidate.",
  "wider_near_turn": "Change only the local quadrature splitting point from hexadecimal 0x1p-20 to 0x1p-7. On [0,cut] the previous enclosure already bounds the remaining 2*q^2/sqrt(q^2+gap) weight by 2*q, and hence bounds its integral by cut^2. The wider bound admits more candidate branches and avoids many expensive Gauss panels. Winding cutoffs, detector limits and RGB policy are unchanged.",
  "limitations": "The catalogue build and one-time screen rows are timed separately from per-star visits. The replay has the full per-sample visit ceiling. Integration must debit actual remaining visits and RGB error in the original footprint so every earlier and later cell is included. CPU and Vulkan proofs have launch enclosures from their respective paths. Frame publication and exact-revision runtime and release qualification remain pending.",
